Did you understand the reference to 'Newton's balls', or is it something 
culture specific?

What happens is that the trap boulder on the left hits the leftmost boulder 
the monk created which shoots past the monk, hits the rightmost boulder 
which goes over the trap and comes to rest on the other side. Then the trap 
triggers again and the boulder on the far right comes shooting back, hits 
the boulder now on the monk's right which shoots past the monk, hits the 
boulder now on his left and knocks the original boulder back to its 
original spot.

All of this is accompanied by copious messages about boulders hitting other 
boulders, and hitting or missing other creatures and my character.

Here's a web page showing the classic Newton's balls:
http://www.phys.ufl.edu/demo/1_Mechanics/N_LinearMomentum/NewtonsBalls.html

